## LoadOnDemand: 1

bootstrap.lua

# File list converted from the old options.xml include manifest.
# Order is load-bearing. ..\H3z0UI\ paths load files from the main addon
# (parent-dir TOC entries are client-supported; Blizzard_PTRFeedbackGlue ships them).
#
# NOTE: LoadOnDemand — ~2.9 MB stays off the login path; the first options
# open pays the compile cost (H3z0UI:EnsureOptionsLoaded, every open path routes
# through it). Login-time theme reads (accent color for layout mode, info bar,
# datatexts) are served by core/theme.lua, which pre-creates H3z0UI.GUI; the
# framework merges into that table on load. The OptionalDeps above only order
# this addon after the login-class module addons when both load (their settings
# builders are loaded here); no builder captures a module symbol at file scope,
# so the ordering is belt-and-suspenders (proven by the headless generator
# smoke test).
search_synonyms.lua
# The generated search index, packed as a long-bracket string (~1.2 MB).
# Loading this file lexes ONE token; framework.lua compiles it on first search.
# It used to be the LoadOnDemand H3z0UI_OptionsSearch addon — one folder for
# one deferral point. Packing gives the same deferral without the folder.
search_cache.lua
framework.lua
border_control.lua
reorder_list.lua
shared.lua
